Keep ownership in one direction.

The worker owns the socket until `sock_alloc_file()` succeeds.
After that, the file owns the socket and cleanup must use `fput()`, not
`sock_release()`.

Publish borrowed pointers only under the mutex.
Timeout and stop may shut them down or signal them, but the worker performs the
matching release.

The helper setup callback runs in the future userspace process.
Reserve exact descriptors 0, 1, and 2, take one file reference for each, then
publish a referenced PID only after all three descriptors are installed.
